# VoiceVision HTTP Server & WebSocket
# Source: src/voicevision/server.py, src/voicevision/websocket.py

## HTTP Server (voicevision-server)
- stdlib only (http.server, json, base64)
- Binds 127.0.0.1:8765 by default
- Optional bearer auth via VOICEVISION_SERVER_TOKEN
- 10 MiB body cap
- Endpoints:
  - GET /health → {"status": "ok", "version": "..."}
  - POST /transcribe → {"audio_base64": "...", "language": "auto|en|pt..."} → {"transcript", "language", "detected_language", "transcription_ms"}
  - POST /describe → {"image_base64": "...", "question": "..."} → {"description"}
  - POST /converse → {"text": "...", "max_tokens": 512} → {"response"}

## WebSocket /stream (websocket.py)
- Minimal RFC 6455 subset (no extensions, no fragmentation)
- Server frames unmasked, client frames masked
- 1 MiB frame cap, 10 MiB audio cap
- Client messages: {"type": "audio", "audio_base64": "...", "language": "..."}
- Client messages: {"type": "end"} / {"type": "reset"}
- Server messages: {"type": "transcript", "transcript": "...", "language": "..."}
- Server messages: {"type": "token", "text": "..."}
- Server messages: {"type": "done"} / {"type": "error", "error": "..."}
- Ping/pong, close codes (1000, 1002, 1003, 1007, 1009)

## VoiceVisionClient (client.py)
- Stdlib only (urllib.request, socket)
- HTTP: health(), transcribe(), describe(), converse()
- WS: stream(chunks) → yields server messages
- Bearer token on both HTTP and WS
- Errors → VoiceVisionClientError with server message